<title>UK: INSIGHT - Gold to consolidate, silver to drift.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT - Gold to consolidate, silver to drift.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p> SPOT     NY CLOSE  * SUPPORT * RESIST * RSI14 *   MA10 *   MA30</p>
<p> GOLD   339.00/9.50 *  336.00 * 342.00 *    38 * 340.29 * 342.51</p>
<p> SILVER   4.77/4.79 *    4.60 *   4.80 *    51 *   4.75 *   4.75</p>
<p> PLAT   411.50/2.50 *  400.00 * 430.00 *    48 * 422.71 * 414.57</p>
<p>-----------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - June 25--------------</p>
<p>Gold is expected to consolidate roughly between $336.00/37.00 and $339.00/40.00 an ounce on Wednesday but will continue to adopt a downside bias against a backdrop of downtrending charts and overhead selling, traders and chartists said.</p>
<p>Silver is set to drift after failing to build a base above $4.80, while platinum and palladium are likely to mirror recent choppy and nervous trading, they added.</p>
